From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 02:53:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] audio/alsa: start the PCM at the threshold's own length, at
 most the buffer

alsa_set_threshold() was given audio_buffer_frames(apdo, &as,
threshold), and audio_buffer_frames() uses the direction's
buffer-length when one is set, in place of the microseconds it is
passed. With out.buffer-length=100000 and threshold=60000 the start
threshold came to 4800 frames at 48 kHz, the whole buffer, not 2880;
and had the device granted a smaller buffer, the start threshold would
have been above it and the PCM would never have started.

Count the threshold's frames from its own microseconds and keep them
to the buffer the device granted.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 audio/alsaaudio.c | 16 +++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/audio/alsaaudio.c b/audio/alsaaudio.c
index a0fdd56d9..cbb0705e5 100644
--- a/audio/alsaaudio.c
+++ b/audio/alsaaudio.c
@@ -533,11 +533,17 @@ static int alsa_open(bool in, struct alsa_params_req *req,
     }
 
     if (!in && aopts->has_threshold && aopts->threshold) {
-        struct audsettings as = { .freq = freq };
-        alsa_set_threshold(
-            handle,
-            audio_buffer_frames(qapi_AudiodevAlsaPerDirectionOptions_base(apdo),
-                                &as, aopts->threshold));
+        /*
+         * The threshold's own length, at most the buffer. audio_buffer_frames()
+         * takes a buffer-length given for the direction in place of the
+         * microseconds it is passed, so with one the threshold was the whole
+         * requested buffer; and a start threshold above the buffer the device
+         * granted never starts the PCM.
+         */
+        snd_pcm_uframes_t frames =
+            ((uint64_t)freq * aopts->threshold + 500000) / 1000000;
+
+        alsa_set_threshold(handle, MIN(frames, obt_buffer_size));
     }
 
     obt->nchannels = nchannels;
